\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces Boxplot of relative absolute error of the single next-timeblock prediction for each of the four surrogate foundation models, grouped by dataset. The models are trained on the same trajectory-datasplit and evaluated in zero-shot fashion on the validation datset. For the flowmatching models, FM-d2 and FM-d3, 16 samples are taken for each input-output pair. The graph mostly the flowmatching model FM-d2 outperforming the other models, except on the pdebench-incomp and pdegym-sines dataset. All models seem to have difficulty predicting the more complex pdebench-comp dataset.}}{25}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ssbox}{{7.1}{25}{Boxplot of relative absolute error of the single next-timeblock prediction for each of the four surrogate foundation models, grouped by dataset. The models are trained on the same trajectory-datasplit and evaluated in zero-shot fashion on the validation datset. For the flowmatching models, FM-d2 and FM-d3, 16 samples are taken for each input-output pair. The graph mostly the flowmatching model FM-d2 outperforming the other models, except on the pdebench-incomp and pdegym-sines dataset. All models seem to have difficulty predicting the more complex pdebench-comp dataset}{figure.caption.21}{}}
